# Cline & Roo Code: Anti-Slop Design Instructions

When designing or modifying user interfaces:
1. Apply the anti-slop rules from `SKILL.md`.
2. Eliminate generic AI styling tropes: no purple glow blobs, no emojis as icons, no vanity stats.
3. Adhere to the 8-pt spatial grid and nested radius math: R_inner = R_outer - Padding.
4. Enforce the 1-to-3 UX hierarchy and page-level controls.
5. Provide 8-state interactive feedback with snappy ease-out transitions (<200ms).
6. Verify WCAG 2.1 AA keyboard focus and contrast before finishing.
